      "abstract": "<jats:title>ABSTRACT</jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>The paper studies, in a general way, how the random properties of a \u2018medium\u2019 influence the percolation of a \u2018fluid\u2019 through it. The treatment diifers from conventional diffusion theory, in which it is the random properties of the fluid that matter. Fluid and medium bear general interpretations: for example, solute diffusing through solvent, electrons migrating over an atomic lattice, molecules penetrating a porous solid, disease infecting a community, etc.</jats:p>",
